      "decision_index": 79,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "By casting Affectionate Indrik before Garruk's Uprising, the player missed the opportunity to sequence Uprising first (this turn, 3 mana) and then Indrik next turn (with 7 mana after playing a land). Casting Uprising first would mean Indrik's ETB next turn triggers Uprising's 'power 4 or greater enters' draw ability, netting an extra card. The cost is taking one attack from Living Lightning (3 damage) with 20 life, which is very manageable.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Affectionate Indrik immediately to fight Living Lightning, without Garruk's Uprising on the battlefield.",
      "better_line": "Cast Garruk's Uprising this turn (3 mana). Next turn, play Evolving Wilds/Forest, then cast Affectionate Indrik (6 mana) to fight Living Lightning while drawing a card from Uprising's trigger.",
